            title: "free and Ownership",
            concept: "free returns memory obtained from malloc to the system, and after free the pointer must not be used again. The code that allocates memory should document who is responsible for freeing it, because unclear ownership causes leaks.",
            syntax: "free(a); a = NULL;",
            exampleCode: "#include <stdio.h>\n\nstatic int fib(int n) {\n    if (n < 2) return n;\n    return fib(n - 1) + fib(n - 2);\n}\n\nint main(void) {\n    printf(\"fib(8): %d\\n\", fib(8));\n    return 0;\n}\n",
