            concept: "A memory leak happens when allocated memory is never freed, so a long-running program slowly uses more and more memory. Every allocation needs a matching free on every path out of the function, including error paths.",
            syntax: "free(a); /* on every exit path */",
            exampleCode: "#include <stdio.h>\n\nint main(void) {\n    int a = 5, b = 6;\n    printf(\"sum: %d\\n\", a + b);\n    printf(\"product: %d\\n\", a * b);\n    return 0;\n}\n",
