            exercise: { title: "Check your understanding of Memory Leaks", type: "multiple-choice", instructions: "Which statement about Memory Leaks is correct?", starterCode: "", solution: "A memory leak happens when allocated memory is never freed, so a long-running program slowly uses more and more memory.", solutionExplanation: "A memory leak happens when allocated memory is never freed, so a long-running program slowly uses more and more memory.", tests: [{ name: "Correct answer", expectedContains: "A memory leak happens when allocated memory is never freed, so a long-running program slowly uses more and more memory.", hidden: false }], hintNotes: { concept: "Remember the key idea of Memory Leaks: A memory leak happens when allocated memory is never freed, so a long-running program slowly uses more and more memory.", approach: "Work in small steps for Memory Leaks: break the task into reading the input, computing the value, and printing only the result in the exact format shown.", structure: "Start from the starter code for Memory Leaks, fill in the missing computation, then run it and compare the output with the expected value." }, options: ["Memory Leaks can only be used once in a program", "Memory Leaks requires a separate paid licence to use", "Memory Leaks is not available in C", "A memory leak happens when allocated memory is never freed, so a long-running program slowly uses more and more memory."], answerIndex: 3 },
