            concept: "Freeing a linked-list stack pops every node until the stack is empty, freeing each node as it goes. An array-based stack needs no freeing, but a stack of pointers must also decide whether the pointed-to data is freed too.",
            syntax: "while (head) { struct Node *t = head; head = head->next; free(t); }",
