            title: "Bubble Sort",
            concept: "Bubble sort repeatedly walks the array swapping neighbours that are out of order, so the largest remaining value bubbles to the end on each pass. It is simple to write but slow, taking quadratic time.",
            syntax: "for (int i = 0; i < n - 1; i++) for (int j = 0; j < n - 1 - i; j++) if (a[j] > a[j + 1]) swap(&a[j], &a[j + 1]);",
            exampleCode: "#include <stdio.h>\n\nint main(void) {\n    int a = 5, b = 6;\n    printf(\"sum: %d\\n\", a + b);\n    printf(\"product: %d\\n\", a * b);\n    return 0;\n}\n",
            exampleLanguage: "c",
