            title: "Recursion and the Stack",
            concept: "Each recursive call uses a stack frame holding its parameters and local variables, so deep recursion can exhaust the call stack. A function that recurses a million levels deep will usually crash with a stack overflow.",
            syntax: "/* each call adds a frame to the call stack */",
            exampleCode: "#include <stdio.h>\n\nint main(void) {\n    int values[] = {4, 9, 14, 19, 7};\n    int max = values[0];\n    for (int i = 1; i < 5; i++) if (values[i] > max) max = values[i];\n    printf(\"max: %d\\n\", max);\n    return 0;\n}\n",
