            title: "errno and perror",
            concept: "errno is a global variable set by library functions when they fail, and perror prints a human-readable message for its current value. errno is only meaningful right after a failing call, because later successful calls may change it.",
            syntax: "if (fopen(path, \"r\") == NULL) { perror(\"fopen\"); }",
