            title: "Error Messages for Users",
            concept: "A good error message says what failed, which input or file was involved, and what the user can do about it. Printing the system error with perror or strerror adds the reason the operating system gives.",
            syntax: "fprintf(stderr, \"cannot open %s: %s\\n\", path, strerror(errno));",
            exampleCode: "#include <stdio.h>\n\nint main(void) {\n    int a = 5, b = 6;\n    printf(\"sum: %d\\n\", a + b);\n    printf(\"product: %d\\n\", a * b);\n    return 0;\n}\n",
            exampleLanguage: "c",
