            id: "c-multi-file-programs-m2-l1",
            slug: "c-multi-file-programs-m2-l1",
            title: "Sharing Variables with extern",
            concept: "A global variable is shared between files by defining it in one source file and declaring it with extern in a header. The extern declaration tells the compiler the variable exists elsewhere.",
            syntax: "extern int counter; /* declaration in header */",
            exampleCode: "#include <stdio.h>\n\nint main(void) {\n    unsigned int x = 128;\n    unsigned int mask = 0x43;\n    printf(\"masked: %u\\n\", x & mask);\n    return 0;\n}\n",
            exampleLanguage: "c",
            mistake: "Defining the same global variable in two files, which causes a link error.",
            bug: { prompt: "The code below copies a string into a fixed buffer without checking its length. Find and fix the bug.", buggyCode: "char buf[16];\nstrcpy(buf, input);", fixedCode: "char buf[16];\nstrncpy(buf, input, sizeof(buf) - 1);\nbuf[sizeof(buf) - 1] = '\\0';", explanation: "strcpy copies without a length limit and can overflow buf; strncpy with an explicit bound plus a terminating NUL keeps the copy inside the buffer." },
            exercise: { title: "Reverse a word for Sharing Variables with extern", type: "test-driven", instructions: "Write a C program that prints a word reversed. This practises Sharing Variables with extern in Multi-File Programs: follow the steps in the starter code and print only the result.", starterCode: "#include <stdio.h>\n#include <string.h>\n\nint main(void) {\n    const char *word = \"sharing_vari\";\n    /* TODO: print the word reversed */\n    return 0;\n}\n", solution: "#include <stdio.h>\n#include <string.h>\n\nint main(void) {\n    const char *word = \"sharing_vari\";\n    size_t n = strlen(word);\n    for (size_t i = n; i > 0; i--) putchar(word[i - 1]);\n    putchar('\\n');\n    return 0;\n}\n", solutionExplanation: "The program prints a word reversed and prints only the result.", tests: [{ name: "Output", expectedStdout: "irav_gnirahs", hidden: false }, { name: "Result appears", expectedContains: "irav_gnirahs", hidden: true }], hintNotes: { concept: "Remember the key idea of Sharing Variables with extern: A global variable is shared between files by defining it in one source file and declaring it with extern in a header.", approach: "Work in small steps for Sharing Variables with extern: break the task into reading the input, computing the value, and printing only the result in the exact format shown.", structure: "Start from the starter code for Sharing Variables with extern, fill in the missing computation, then run it and compare the output with the expected value." } },
