            slug: "c-multi-file-programs-m2-l3",
            title: "Compiling Multiple Files",
            concept: "Compiling several source files means compiling each one to an object file and then linking the objects together into one program. A single gcc command can do both steps, or the steps can be run separately.",
            syntax: "gcc -c math.c && gcc -c main.c && gcc math.o main.o -o app",
            exampleCode: "#include <stdio.h>\n\nint main(void) {\n    int a = 5, b = 6;\n    printf(\"sum: %d\\n\", a + b);\n    printf(\"product: %d\\n\", a * b);\n    return 0;\n}\n",
