            title: "Testing Pointer Code",
            concept: "Testing pointer code means checking that the function returns the right values and that it does not leak, double-free, or write out of bounds. Running the tests under Valgrind or AddressSanitizer catches the memory errors that plain assertions miss.",
            syntax: "/* run tests under valgrind to catch leaks */",
