            title: "Function Pointers vs Switch",
            concept: "A dispatch table of function pointers is easier to extend than a switch, because adding an operation means adding an entry instead of editing a long chain of cases. A switch is clearer when there are only a few cases and they rarely change.",
            syntax: "/* table: easy to extend; switch: easy to read for few cases */",
            exampleCode: "#include <stdio.h>\n#include <string.h>\n\nint main(void) {\n    const char *word = \"example\";\n    printf(\"length of %s: %zu\\n\", word, strlen(word));\n    return 0;\n}\n",
