            concept: "A tagged union pairs a union with an enum tag that records which member currently holds a valid value, so the program can check the tag before reading. The tag is what makes a union safe to use.",
            syntax: "struct Value { enum Kind kind; union { int i; double d; } u; };",
            exampleCode: "#include <stdio.h>\n\nint main(void) {\n    int a = 5, b = 6;\n    printf(\"sum: %d\\n\", a + b);\n    printf(\"product: %d\\n\", a * b);\n    return 0;\n}\n",
