            slug: "c-preprocessor-m1-l1",
            title: "What the Preprocessor Does",
            concept: "The preprocessor runs before the compiler and handles directives such as #include, #define and #ifdef by transforming the source text. It works on text, not on C code, which is why its rules sometimes surprise beginners.",
            syntax: "/* the preprocessor runs before compilation */",
            exampleCode: "#include <stdio.h>\n\nint main(void) {\n    int total = 0;\n    for (int i = 1; i <= 5; i++) total += i;\n    printf(\"total: %d\\n\", total);\n    return 0;\n}\n",
