            concept: "Copying a string safely means knowing the size of the destination and never writing past it, which strncpy and snprintf guarantee when used correctly. The copy must always end with a NUL terminator.",
            syntax: "strncpy(dst, src, sizeof(dst) - 1); dst[sizeof(dst) - 1] = '\\0';",
            exampleCode: "#include <stdio.h>\n\nstatic int fib(int n) {\n    if (n < 2) return n;\n    return fib(n - 1) + fib(n - 2);\n}\n\nint main(void) {\n    printf(\"fib(8): %d\\n\", fib(8));\n    return 0;\n}\n",
