            title: "Traversing Without Looping Forever",
            concept: "Traversing a circular list starts at a chosen node and stops when it comes back to that node, because there is no NULL to stop at. A do-while loop fits this shape, since the starting node must be visited once.",
            syntax: "do { visit(p); p = p->next; } while (p != head);",
