            slug: "c-circular-lists-m1-l4",
            title: "Deleting from a Circular List",
            concept: "Deleting from a circular list means linking the predecessor around the removed node and, if the removed node was the starting node, choosing a new start. Deleting the last remaining node leaves the list empty.",
            syntax: "prev->next = cur->next; if (cur == head) head = cur->next;",
            exampleCode: "#include <stdio.h>\n\nstatic int fib(int n) {\n    if (n < 2) return n;\n    return fib(n - 1) + fib(n - 2);\n}\n\nint main(void) {\n    printf(\"fib(8): %d\\n\", fib(8));\n    return 0;\n}\n",
