            title: "Array-Based Deques",
            concept: "An array-based deque is a circular buffer with front and rear indices that can move in either direction, wrapping around with modulo arithmetic. Both ends grow towards each other, so the buffer is full when they meet.",
            syntax: "front = (front - 1 + MAX) % MAX; /* push front */",
            exampleCode: "#include <stdio.h>\n\nint main(void) {\n    unsigned int x = 128;\n    unsigned int mask = 0x43;\n    printf(\"masked: %u\\n\", x & mask);\n    return 0;\n}\n",
