            title: "Quadratic Time",
            concept: "Quadratic time, O(n squared), means the cost grows with the square of the input size, which happens with nested loops over the same data, such as bubble sort. Doubling the input quadruples the work.",
            syntax: "/* nested loops over n items: about n squared steps */",
            exampleCode: "#include <stdio.h>\n\nint main(void) {\n    unsigned int x = 128;\n    unsigned int mask = 0x43;\n    printf(\"masked: %u\\n\", x & mask);\n    return 0;\n}\n",
