            bug: { prompt: "The code below copies a string into a fixed buffer without checking its length. Find and fix the bug.", buggyCode: "char buf[16];\nstrcpy(buf, input);", fixedCode: "char buf[16];\nstrncpy(buf, input, sizeof(buf) - 1);\nbuf[sizeof(buf) - 1] = '\\0';", explanation: "strcpy copies without a length limit and can overflow buf; strncpy with an explicit bound plus a terminating NUL keeps the copy inside the buffer." },
            exercise: { title: "Greatest common divisor for Quadratic Time", type: "test-driven", instructions: "Write a C program that reads two integers from standard input and prints their greatest common divisor. This practises Quadratic Time in Algorithm Complexity and Big-O: follow the steps in the starter code and print only the result.", starterCode: "#include <stdio.h>\n\nint main(void) {\n    int a, b;\n    if (scanf(\"%d %d\", &a, &b) != 2) return 1;\n    /* TODO: print the gcd */\n    return 0;\n}\n", solution: "#include <stdio.h>\n\nint main(void) {\n    int a, b;\n    if (scanf(\"%d %d\", &a, &b) != 2) return 1;\n    while (b != 0) { int t = a % b; a = b; b = t; }\n    printf(\"%d\\n\", a);\n    return 0;\n}\n", solutionExplanation: "The program reads two integers from standard input and prints their greatest common divisor and prints only the result.", tests: [{ name: "Example input", stdin: "48 36\n", expectedStdout: "12", hidden: false }, { name: "Second input", stdin: "51 41\n", expectedStdout: "1", hidden: true }], hintNotes: { concept: "Remember the key idea of Quadratic Time: Quadratic time, O(n squared), means the cost grows with the square of the input size, which happens with nested loops over the same data, such as bubble sort.", approach: "Work in small steps for Quadratic Time: break the task into reading the input, computing the value, and printing only the result in the exact format shown.", structure: "Start from the starter code for Quadratic Time, fill in the missing computation, then run it and compare the output with the expected value." } },
